<div class="card"><h5>The Daily Flow</h5>
<p><strong>Morning:</strong> Open the Dashboard to see today's prayer times, your next prayer and today's tasks. Add anything missing in My Day.</p>
<p><strong>During the day:</strong> Mark each prayer on the Salah page after you pray. Log water with the quick-add buttons, meals after you eat, and walking or exercise when you finish. Mark office attendance and log freelance work as it happens.</p>
<p class="mb-0"><strong>Night:</strong> Start (or record) your sleep, tick off your habits, and open Reports to see your whole day — tasks, prayers, water, money and more.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Tasks (My Day)</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: your daily to-do list and routine. How to use: tap Add Task, write a clear title, pick a date, category and priority. Choose a Repeat option (daily, weekly, weekdays, monthly) for routine tasks — the app creates a separate copy for each day, so yesterday's history never changes. Tap Complete when done; Postpone moves a task to tomorrow, Duplicate copies it. Your data appears on the Dashboard, in My Day, on the Calendar and in Reports.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>My Routine (the repeating plan)</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: the plan that repeats — your normal day, built once. How it is different from Tasks: a task is one job on one day; a routine activity creates a fresh copy of itself in My Day on every day it repeats (every day, weekdays, custom days and so on). Edit the routine and only future days change — yesterday keeps its own history. Use My Routine for waking, learning, exercise, office-time blocks and sleep; use Tasks for one-time jobs. Working days vs days off: choose "Weekdays (Monday to Friday)" for workday activities and specific custom days for weekend-only ones.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Salah</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: the five daily prayer times for your city (calculated from your coordinates — never hardcoded) with a status record for each prayer. How to use: after each prayer, choose Waqt par, Late, Qaza or Missed and tap Save; you may also note the time you prayed. Leave a prayer Unmarked if you have not prayed yet — the app never marks a prayer missed by itself. Calculation convention (Fajr/Isha), the Hanafi Asr method and small minute adjustments live in Salah Settings. Your data appears on the Dashboard, in Salah History, on the Calendar and in Reports.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Health — Water, Weight, Walking, Exercise</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: simple daily health tracking. How to use: Water — tap +250 ml / +500 ml / +750 ml / +1 litre when you drink, or Add for an exact amount. Weight — add one entry whenever you weigh yourself; every entry is kept, so your trend chart is real history. Walking — log distance (and steps/duration if you know them). Exercise — log each session with its type and minutes; multiple sessions per day are fine. Targets (water ml, walking km, target weight) are set in Settings. Your data appears on the Dashboard, in Health lists and in Reports.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Meals</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: a simple food diary. How to use: after eating, tap Add Meal, choose Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner or Snack, and write the food name — quantity can go in the name, e.g. “2 rotis + daal”. Tick Home-cooked, or untick it for outside food. Exact calories are not required; nutrition numbers are optional and are only your own estimates. Your data appears in the Meals list, on the Calendar and in Reports.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Sleep</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: your sleep record with start time, wake-up time, duration and quality. How to use: tap “Start Sleep Now” when you go to sleep and “Wake Up / End Sleep” when you wake, or use Manual Entry for a past sleep. Sleep can cross midnight — starting at 6:00 AM and waking at 2:00 PM is recorded correctly, and the duration is calculated for you. Your data appears in the Sleep list, on the Dashboard and in Reports.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Office</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: attendance, working hours, late arrival, leaves and salary history for your job. How to use: add one record per working day with your start and end times — overnight shifts that end the next day (e.g. 5:00 PM to 2:00 AM) are supported, and total hours and late arrival are worked out from your office timings in Settings. For a leave day, tick Leave instead of times. Record each salary with the form on the Office page when you receive it. Your data appears in the Office list and monthly summaries.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Freelancing</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: your freelance projects and the income they bring. How to use: add each project with its client, platform and status, and update the status as work moves; fill Actual Revenue when you are paid. Separately, log every payment in Freelance Income with gross amount and fees — net income (gross − fees) is calculated for you. If a payment is in another currency, keep its original currency; the optional exchange rate is only used to show a combined estimate. Your data appears in the Projects and Income lists and in Reports.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Learning</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: your courses, skills and study time. How to use: first add a Goal/Course (what you want to learn, with a target date if you have one). Each time you study, Log Session with the topic and minutes, optionally linked to the goal. Update the goal's progress % as you go and mark it Completed when you finish. Your data appears in the Learning lists and as learning minutes in Reports.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Habits</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: a daily checklist for habits you are building, like a morning walk or reading. How to use: create a habit with a clear target (what counts as “done”), then tap Mark Done each day you do it. Every day is stored separately, so streaks and history stay correct even if you later pause or edit the habit. Your data appears in the Habits list, on the Calendar and in Reports.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Finance</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: personal income and expense tracking — this is a private record for you only; it does not connect to any bank. How to use: add one entry for each income (Salary, Freelancing) or expense (Food, Transport, Bills, Family, Health, Education, Entertainment, Shopping, Other) with the amount and date. Reports then show your monthly totals, category breakdown and net savings. Your data appears in the Finance list, on the Calendar and in Reports.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Calendar</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: everything you recorded, organised by date. How to use: pick any date to see that day's tasks, prayers, meals, sleep, exercise, finance, learning and habits together, and use the month overview to spot busy or empty days. To correct a past day, open the record from its own section and edit it — the original creation information is kept.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Reports</h5><p class="mb-0">What it is: daily, weekly, monthly, yearly and custom-date summaries with charts, all calculated from your real records — nothing is sample or estimated data. How to use: open a report, choose Daily/Weekly/Monthly/Yearly from the top, or pick your own From and To dates in Custom. Weekly also compares you with the previous week. Use Print → Save as PDF in your browser if you want a PDF copy.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Notifications & Reminders</h5>
<p>How reminders work: the server checks your reminders every minute (this needs the scheduler/cron to be running on the server). Prayer reminders come from your Salah settings, task reminders from each task's “minutes before”, and you can add your own reminders (for example water or exercise) in Settings → Notifications. Every sent reminder is logged, so the same reminder is never sent twice.</p>
<p>Ways you can receive them: in-app, from the notification bell/inbox in the app; and as Web Push on your device, if the app is installed (PWA) and you have allowed notification permission. Push also needs VAPID keys configured on the server by whoever hosts the app. On iPhone, first add the app to the Home Screen (Share → Add to Home Screen, iOS 16.4 or later), open it from the Home Screen icon, and then allow notifications.</p>
<p class="mb-0">To test it: go to Settings → Notifications, tap Enable Notifications and allow permission, then add a custom reminder for the current time — it should arrive within about a minute while the scheduler is running. If permission was denied, the app still works fully; reminders simply stay in-app.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Appearance (Dark, Light, System)</h5><p class="mb-0">Settings → Appearance changes how the whole app looks: Dark is the original theme, Light is bright for daylight, and System follows your phone or computer automatically. You can also pick an accent color — buttons, links, graphs and progress bars change with it. Your choice is saved to your account, so it is the same on every device and stays after refresh.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Privacy</h5><p class="mb-0">Every record belongs to your account only. No other user can see, open or edit your data — opening another account's record is blocked. Your data is stored in the app's database (the server is the source of truth, not just your phone), and you can download a full export of everything at any time from Settings → Export & Backup.</p></div>

<div class="card"><h5>Going Live</h5><p class="mb-0">When you move the app from your own computer to your hosting, follow the included guides: the README for setup, <em>docs/HOSTINGER_DEPLOYMENT.md</em> for step-by-step Hostinger deployment (document root, database, storage link and the cron line for reminders), <em>docs/DATABASE_SCHEMA.md</em> for the database design, <em>docs/FEATURE_CHECKLIST.md</em> for what is included, and <em>docs/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md</em> for honest limitations, including iPhone push notes.</p></div>
